### (3/7) Preserve binary fallback for malformed sample bytes
**Severity:** `medium`

Malformed UTF-8 can be encountered while reading the initial sample. Catch that decoder failure and expose the original file as a StorageItem instead of returning replacement-decoded text.

```suggestion
        int sampleLength;
        try
        {
            sampleLength = await reader.ReadAsync(sample.AsMemory(), cancellationToken);
        }
        catch (DecoderFallbackException)
        {
            return await CreateFilePackageViewAsync(package, inputFile);
        }

```

### (6/7) Preserve fallback for malformed bytes after the sample
**Severity:** `medium`

Invalid UTF-8 can occur after the initial sample as well. Apply the same binary fallback around the bounded remainder read so partial text is not returned for a malformed file.

```suggestion
        try
        {
            textBuilder.Append(await ReadBoundedAsync(reader, maximumTextCharacters - sampleLength, cancellationToken));
        }
        catch (DecoderFallbackException)
        {
            return await CreateFilePackageViewAsync(package, inputFile);
        }

```

### (7/7) Share the binary-file package fallback
**Severity:** `medium`

The non-text and decoder-failure branches need to create the same StorageItem-backed package. Add one helper for that shared behavior and retain the existing bounded reader below it.

```suggestion
    private static async Task<DataPackageView> CreateFilePackageViewAsync(DataPackage package, FileInfo inputFile)
    {
        var storageFile = await StorageFile.GetFileFromPathAsync(inputFile.FullName);
        package.SetStorageItems([storageFile]);
        return package.GetView();
    }

    private static async Task<string> ReadBoundedAsync(TextReader reader, int maximumCharacters, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
```

### Apply the OpenAI policy to unknown provider types
**Severity:** `high`

`IsProviderAllowed` leaves `AIServiceType.Unknown` unchanged and the switch falls through to `true`, but provider construction normalizes that value to OpenAI. An unknown-configured provider can therefore pass this policy check while OpenAI is disabled. Normalize before metadata lookup and the provider-specific GPO switch.

```suggestion
        var serviceType = provider.ServiceType.ToAIServiceType();
        if (serviceType == AIServiceType.Unknown)
        {
            serviceType = AIServiceType.OpenAI;
        }

```

### (1/3) Check policy before building the CLI host
**Severity:** `medium`

`Main` constructs the engine host before checking whether Advanced Paste is disabled. Return the stable policy error before host initialization so the disabled CLI does not load the engine.

```suggestion
        if (TryWritePolicyDisabledError(args, Console.Error, AdvancedPastePolicy.IsAdvancedPasteEnabled))
        {
            LogCLITelemetry(GetTelemetryCommandName(args), successful: false, loggerInitialized: false);
            return RuntimeErrorExitCode;
        }

        using var cancellationSource = new CancellationTokenSource();
```

### (2/3) Guard the actions-list path
**Severity:** `medium`

The actions-list branch returns descriptors before `ExecuteAsync` applies its policy guard. Use the same stable disabled-policy response before listing action identifiers.

```suggestion
        if (TryWritePolicyDisabledError(args, stderr, AdvancedPastePolicy.IsAdvancedPasteEnabled))
        {
            return RuntimeErrorExitCode;
        }

        if (parseResult.CommandResult.Command.Name == "list")
```

### (3/3) Reuse one stable disabled-policy response
**Severity:** `medium`

Both entry points need the same JSON-or-human-readable `disabled_by_policy` response. Add one helper so the startup and list guards cannot drift.

```suggestion
    internal static bool TryWritePolicyDisabledError(string[] args, TextWriter stderr, bool policyEnabled)
    {
        if (policyEnabled)
        {
            return false;
        }

        WriteError(stderr, IsJsonRequested(args), "disabled_by_policy", "Advanced Paste is disabled by policy.");
        return true;
    }

    internal static bool TryInitializeLogger(Action initializeLogger)
```

